WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:06.550
Go, Sam Obisanya.
Go, Sam Obisanya.

2
00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:09.302
Today has been all about one man.

3
00:00:11.304 --> 00:00:16.308
Take a bow, Sam Obisanya.
The first hat trick of his career.

4
00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:18.061
Three goals for Obisanya.

5
00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:22.732
Three points for Richmond
as their incredible run of form continues.

6
00:00:22.816 --> 00:00:25.485
They will now enter
the final match of the season

7
00:00:25.569 --> 00:00:29.364
one win away
from promotion back to the Premier League.

8
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:32.033
An incredible turnaround.

9
00:00:32.909 --> 00:00:34.786
Thataway, Sam!

10
00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:37.998
What a performance by
the young Nigerian, Chris.

11
00:00:38.081 --> 00:00:41.334
It's exciting to see a young player
realizing his potential, Arlo.

12
00:00:43.044 --> 00:00:45.839
-One more, one more. One more.
-All right, bro. See you later.

13
00:00:45.922 --> 00:00:48.091
See you later. All right. Peace.

14
00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:50.635
Yeah.

15
00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:51.928
-Bravo, Sam.
-Three goals.

16
00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:54.514
-All right. See you later.
-That's gold. That's it, dude.

17
00:00:54.598 --> 00:00:56.975
-Congratulations, Sam. Well done.
-Thank you, Liza.

18
00:00:57.058 --> 00:00:58.101
See you later.

19
00:01:25.378 --> 00:01:26.379
Well done, matey.

20
00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:36.973
Wish me luck.

21
00:01:56.493 --> 00:01:57.619
Watch out!

22
00:02:24.521 --> 00:02:26.398
I can't believe it's happening.

23
00:02:26.481 --> 00:02:28.316
The whole idea of it has got me
going like…

24
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.402
Oh, stop. You getting all…

25
00:02:31.486 --> 00:02:34.114
is just fear getting in the way
of what you deserve.

26
00:02:34.698 --> 00:02:36.116
Are you making fun of me with my…

27
00:02:36.866 --> 00:02:37.909
Of course not.

28
00:02:37.993 --> 00:02:40.912
It's just, you went…
And I thought I can't improve on that.

29
00:02:40.996 --> 00:02:42.330
I'm just gonna have to replicate it.

30
00:02:43.206 --> 00:02:44.374
Thank you.

31
00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:46.585
Bing-bong, you ding-dongs.

32
00:02:46.668 --> 00:02:47.961
-Ted.
-Yeah?

33
00:02:48.044 --> 00:02:51.882
Guess who is going to be featured
in Vanity Fair's business issue

34
00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:53.508
as a powerful woman on the rise.

35
00:02:53.592 --> 00:02:55.552
I finally got it? This is incredible!

36
00:02:55.635 --> 00:02:57.053
-Ted.
-Yeah?

37
00:02:57.137 --> 00:02:58.805
Not you. Keeley.

38
00:02:58.889 --> 00:03:00.891
Oh, that makes more sense.
Hey, congrats, Keeley.

39
00:03:00.974 --> 00:03:02.559
That's gonna be a Vanity Fair to remember.

40
00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:05.896
Oh, it's just an honor
to be mad fit and successful.

41
00:03:05.979 --> 00:03:07.397
Yeah.

42
00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:13.236
So, ladies, I'm here
both to give and receive.

43
00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.988
Dr. Sharon's last day is tomorrow,

44
00:03:15.071 --> 00:03:16.406
and we're all chipping in
to get her something special.

45
00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:18.950
-What did you decide on?
-An envelope of cash.

46
00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.120
You know, I figured she already has
all our deep, dark secrets.

47
00:03:22.203 --> 00:03:24.831
Kinda tough to top that
with a scarf and a candle, you know?

48
00:03:24.915 --> 00:03:26.249
Right.

49
00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:28.335
-Yeah. Whatever you got.
-Let's see.

50
00:03:28.418 --> 00:03:29.920
Oh, you know what? Here you go.

51
00:03:30.003 --> 00:03:31.296
Lovely. Thank you.

52
00:03:32.422 --> 00:03:33.548
Yeah.

53
00:03:33.632 --> 00:03:35.383
Yeah. It all spends the same.

54
00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:36.718
All right. Appreciate you.

55
00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.178
-Hello, people.
-Higgins!

56
00:03:38.261 --> 00:03:39.095
Leslie.

57
00:03:39.179 --> 00:03:42.057
I just received an email from Edwin Akufo,

58
00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:45.477
and he wants to speak with you, Rebecca.

59
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.853
Okay.

60
00:03:46.937 --> 00:03:47.938
Who is Edwin Akufo?

61
00:03:48.772 --> 00:03:51.858
His father owns
the largest tech firm in Ghana.

62
00:03:51.942 --> 00:03:53.318
Wait a second. I thought I did.

63
00:03:53.401 --> 00:03:54.569
Until he died last month.

64
00:03:54.653 --> 00:03:55.820
I apologize for my joke.

65
00:03:56.404 --> 00:04:01.034
Edwin just inherited £1.2 billion
and loves football.

66
00:04:02.494 --> 00:04:03.578
And?

67
00:04:04.162 --> 00:04:06.998
And I think he wants to buy the club.

68
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.218
Hi. Got the suit Ted bought you
back from the dry cleaners.

69
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.511
Oh, it's my suit.

70
00:04:20.262 --> 00:04:21.513
The second Ted gave it to me,

71
00:04:21.596 --> 00:04:23.682
ownership transferred,
and it became my suit, Will.

72
00:04:24.641 --> 00:04:25.642
Right.

73
00:04:30.105 --> 00:04:32.315
Oi, are my eyebrows crazy?

74
00:04:34.776 --> 00:04:36.903
I've gotta do a photo shoot
with Keeley tonight,

75
00:04:36.987 --> 00:04:40.782
and the photo shoot coordinator told me
my eyebrows are crazy.

76
00:04:41.866 --> 00:04:43.743
Jesus, are my eyebrows crazy?

77
00:04:43.827 --> 00:04:47.038
They wanna do a "at home
with the footballer boyfriend" shot.

78
00:04:47.664 --> 00:04:49.416
Bet they won't even use it.

79
00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:53.128
She also told me I've gotta wear all black
so that Keeley pops.

80
00:04:53.211 --> 00:04:55.422
-You're always wearing black.
-This isn't black.

81
00:04:55.505 --> 00:04:57.007
This is dark heather charcoal.

82
00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.509
I love hearing fellas debate fashion.
Who's winning?

83
00:05:00.051 --> 00:05:02.554
Oh, Ted,
can I run a new tactic by you?

84
00:05:02.637 --> 00:05:05.098
Yeah, you can run it, walk it,
cartwheel it to me. I don't care.

85
00:05:05.181 --> 00:05:06.808
Call me Dumbo, 'cause I'm all ears.

86
00:05:06.892 --> 00:05:08.310
-Is that a yes?
-Yes.

87
00:05:08.393 --> 00:05:11.980
Okay. When we play Brentford,
we should play with a false nine.

88
00:05:12.063 --> 00:05:14.691
-Couldn't agree more. What is that?
-Play without strikers.

89
00:05:14.774 --> 00:05:16.818
Okay.
Wait, so Jamie and Dani ain't gonna play?

90
00:05:16.902 --> 00:05:19.946
They do, but they play in midfield
where no one expects them to be.

91
00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.031
-Yeah.
-I see.

92
00:05:21.114 --> 00:05:23.617
Okay, so we got both our aces
tucked up our sleeves, huh?

93
00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:25.744
Love that. That's fun.

94
00:05:25.827 --> 00:05:28.496
Okay, today let's go ahead
and try out your fake nine.

95
00:05:29.539 --> 00:05:30.540
False nine.

96
00:05:30.624 --> 00:05:32.250
-Hey, this looks very nice.
-Thank you.

97
00:05:33.293 --> 00:05:34.294
Here we go again.

98
00:05:35.378 --> 00:05:37.714
Give Ted yet another idea
he'll take all the credit for.

99
00:05:39.925 --> 00:05:40.926
That's the job, son.

100
00:05:42.135 --> 00:05:43.803
Do you guys ever wanna be in charge?

101
00:05:43.887 --> 00:05:45.096
Be the boss?

102
00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.473
Get all the credit?

103
00:05:51.061 --> 00:05:54.606
You know, we used to believe that
trees competed with each other for light.

104
00:05:54.689 --> 00:05:56.650
Suzanne Simard's field work
challenged that perception,

105
00:05:56.733 --> 00:05:59.694
and we now realize that
the forest is a socialist community.

106
00:05:59.778 --> 00:06:02.489
Trees work in harmony
to share the sunlight.

107
00:06:03.406 --> 00:06:05.575
Can't you just give me
a straight answer for once?

108
00:06:06.159 --> 00:06:07.202
I think he just did.

109
00:06:09.204 --> 00:06:12.249
Right. When this works, which it will,

110
00:06:12.332 --> 00:06:15.001
I'm telling everyone it was my idea,
which it was.

111
00:06:18.672 --> 00:06:20.048
Your eyebrows aren't crazy.

112
00:06:20.131 --> 00:06:21.174
Thank you.

113
00:06:21.258 --> 00:06:22.467
They're psychotic.

114
00:06:22.551 --> 00:06:23.969
I appreciate that.

115
00:06:28.014 --> 00:06:29.683
They can't maintain their lines.

116
00:06:31.393 --> 00:06:33.687
-These guys are just not in sync.
-It's okay.

117
00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.897
Oh, hell no. No, no. Hey, hey.

118
00:06:36.481 --> 00:06:38.858
No. No, no. Guys, come on.
That ain't gonna cut it.

119
00:06:38.942 --> 00:06:41.403
Y'all gotta be together on this,
all right? It's like this.

120
00:06:41.486 --> 00:06:45.448
You may hate me,
but it ain't no lie. Yeah?

121
00:06:45.532 --> 00:06:48.368
Then the hands. Bye, bye, bye. All right?

122
00:06:48.451 --> 00:06:50.870
And watch my jumps. Ain't no lie.

123
00:06:50.954 --> 00:06:52.747
See how I'm jumping?
Like I'm a marionette.

124
00:06:52.831 --> 00:06:55.959
That's why this song is on the album
No Strings Attached, all right?

125
00:06:56.585 --> 00:06:58.253
Yes. Okay, good.

126
00:06:58.336 --> 00:07:00.630
Now, look, fellas, performing this
at Doc's going-away party

127
00:07:00.714 --> 00:07:02.549
ain't gonna mean Bo Jackson diddly squat

128
00:07:02.632 --> 00:07:04.759
unless she can tell
how hard we worked on it.

129
00:07:04.843 --> 00:07:06.386
You know what I mean?

130
00:07:06.469 --> 00:07:09.014
It ain't the execution.
That ain't the gift. It's the effort.

131
00:07:09.097 --> 00:07:11.433
Yeah? Okay? You see what I mean?

132
00:07:15.228 --> 00:07:16.563
Uh-oh.

133
00:07:47.802 --> 00:07:48.803
Okay.

134
00:07:52.015 --> 00:07:53.016
Okay.

135
00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.398
My most sincere apologies.

136
00:08:00.482 --> 00:08:02.275
I was told your training
would be finished by now.

137
00:08:02.359 --> 00:08:04.945
Oh, that's okay. Hakuna matata, right?

138
00:08:06.112 --> 00:08:08.365
Oh, I'm sorry.
That was kind of racist, wasn't it?

139
00:08:08.448 --> 00:08:11.409
Oh, you know,
Timon and Pumbaa are cartoons.

140
00:08:11.493 --> 00:08:13.453
-So I'll let it slide.
-Hey, I appreciate you.

141
00:08:14.704 --> 00:08:15.872
So, you must be Edwin Akufo, huh?

142
00:08:15.956 --> 00:08:16.915
-Yeah, I am.
-I'm Ted Lasso.

143
00:08:16.998 --> 00:08:18.541
I don't shake hands.

144
00:08:19.542 --> 00:08:21.253
But I have someone who does. Francis.

145
00:08:21.336 --> 00:08:22.420
-Oh. Hi.
-Yes.

146
00:08:27.384 --> 00:08:30.220
That is one of the best handshakes
I've ever hand shook right there.

147
00:08:30.303 --> 00:08:33.932
Firm yet comforting, you know,
like a weighted blanket for my hand toes.

148
00:08:34.015 --> 00:08:36.226
So, I bet you're looking to chop it up
with Miss Welton, yeah?

149
00:08:36.308 --> 00:08:37.435
If that's not impossible.

150
00:08:37.519 --> 00:08:40.855
Well, you say impossible,
but all I hear is "I'm possible."

151
00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:44.693
Makes more sense when written down.

152
00:08:44.776 --> 00:08:45.860
-Okay.
-Yeah.

153
00:08:45.944 --> 00:08:47.654
-Right this way, fellas.
-Thank you.

154
00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:50.532
-Take it from here?
-If it's gotta be me.

155
00:08:51.741 --> 00:08:54.744
Okay, Greyhounds,
now let's get in formation!

156
00:08:55.537 --> 00:08:57.080
Will, here we go!

157
00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:02.377
Five, six, seven, eight.

158
00:09:04.337 --> 00:09:05.338
Come on.

159
00:09:06.464 --> 00:09:07.465
Good.

160
00:09:10.385 --> 00:09:11.636
Hit this.

161
00:09:20.562 --> 00:09:21.563
That was it!

162
00:09:30.614 --> 00:09:31.948
Yes!

163
00:09:32.032 --> 00:09:35.201
I cannot tell you how much I admire
what your club has done this season.

164
00:09:35.285 --> 00:09:37.537
Relegation destroys some teams,

165
00:09:37.621 --> 00:09:39.539
but it's only seemed to
have made yours stronger.

166
00:09:39.623 --> 00:09:42.792
That's all 'cause of the boss right here.
Trickle-down economics may stink,

167
00:09:42.876 --> 00:09:44.920
but trickle-down support
smells like pizza,

168
00:09:45.003 --> 00:09:46.463
roses and, I assume, Viola Davis.

169
00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.925
I do care about this club, Mr. Akufo.

170
00:09:50.008 --> 00:09:51.009
Very much.

171
00:09:51.092 --> 00:09:52.802
That's why I'll cut straight to the point

172
00:09:52.886 --> 00:09:54.554
and tell you that
I'm not interested in selling.

173
00:09:55.138 --> 00:09:56.848
Oh, I'm not trying to buy your club.

174
00:09:58.058 --> 00:10:00.101
I'm interested in buying
one of your players.

175
00:10:01.061 --> 00:10:02.604
Sam Obisanya.

176
00:10:04.397 --> 00:10:05.899
But Rebecca loves Sam.

177
00:10:06.942 --> 00:10:08.193
Yeah, we all love Sam.

178
00:10:08.276 --> 00:10:09.402
Exactly.

179
00:10:10.028 --> 00:10:13.823
Also, Sam is under contract
with us for another three years.

180
00:10:13.907 --> 00:10:15.200
Yes, I understand.

181
00:10:15.283 --> 00:10:17.702
Therefore, I would offer you
a generous transfer fee

182
00:10:17.786 --> 00:10:20.038
of so much money
that people would think I'm crazy,

183
00:10:20.121 --> 00:10:21.957
and you've taken advantage of me,

184
00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.000
in a financial, non-sexual way, of course.

185
00:10:25.627 --> 00:10:27.963
I believe he's making you
an offer you can't refuse.

186
00:10:28.046 --> 00:10:29.339
Oh, Godfather, I see you.

187
00:10:30.423 --> 00:10:33.301
Well, I'm refusing an offer he can't make.

188
00:10:34.803 --> 00:10:36.388
Is that a quote from the third movie?

189
00:10:37.305 --> 00:10:38.807
I just have one question.

190
00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.642
What club is it that you actually own?

191
00:10:40.725 --> 00:10:41.810
Oh, I don't.

192
00:10:42.394 --> 00:10:44.187
At least, not one I can talk about yet.

193
00:10:44.271 --> 00:10:46.273
But it is a team in Africa,

194
00:10:46.356 --> 00:10:49.568
and I figured that Sam might appreciate
the opportunity to play near his family.

195
00:10:49.651 --> 00:10:50.902
You know, his home.

196
00:10:53.905 --> 00:10:56.866
Well, gosh dang it.
Now I wish we had two Sams, you know?

197
00:10:58.159 --> 00:10:59.411
One for y'all and one for us.

198
00:10:59.494 --> 00:11:01.371
Where are we at with cloning these days,
by the way?

199
00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:04.457
Them Scottish folks have been
mighty quiet on that front for a while,

200
00:11:04.541 --> 00:11:05.875
which means we gotta be close, right?

201
00:11:05.959 --> 00:11:09.129
Yeah, well, like my father used to say,
a sad white man is still a white man.

202
00:11:09.212 --> 00:11:10.297
Word.

203
00:11:12.007 --> 00:11:14.926
All I'm asking is for
an opportunity to speak to Sam.

204
00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:16.761
Maybe let him decide for himself, yes?

205
00:11:17.345 --> 00:11:18.346
Yes.

206
00:11:20.807 --> 00:11:22.976
Oh, I hope I'm not interrupting.

207
00:11:23.059 --> 00:11:24.394
Perfect timing.

208
00:11:25.061 --> 00:11:28.106
Sam, this is Edwin Akufo.

209
00:11:30.609 --> 00:11:32.068
Oh, he doesn't like to shake--

210
00:11:36.323 --> 00:11:38.533
Mr. Akufo would like to speak with you.

211
00:11:38.617 --> 00:11:41.661
I figure we could
maybe go to a museum,

212
00:11:41.745 --> 00:11:43.246
have something to eat.

213
00:11:44.289 --> 00:11:45.290
Sure.

214
00:11:45.373 --> 00:11:47.375
Wonderful. After you.

215
00:11:47.459 --> 00:11:48.710
Okay.

216
00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.131
It's lovely to meet you all.

217
00:11:53.715 --> 00:11:54.716
-Bye.
-You too.

218
00:11:59.304 --> 00:12:00.472
So strange.

219
00:12:00.555 --> 00:12:03.058
I once wrote a play about a billionaire

220
00:12:03.141 --> 00:12:06.228
who took a footballer
to a museum and then dinner.

221
00:12:08.188 --> 00:12:09.439
What happens in the play?

222
00:12:09.522 --> 00:12:10.815
Well, they get their meal for free

223
00:12:10.899 --> 00:12:13.318
because they found
a little bit of glass in the pasta.

224
00:12:16.529 --> 00:12:17.989
God, I wish I could write fiction.

225
00:12:18.073 --> 00:12:22.202
Oh, thank you, Keeley.
You know, I should revisit that work.

226
00:12:22.285 --> 00:12:23.286
Yeah.

227
00:12:27.749 --> 00:12:30.001
Hi. No.

228
00:12:30.835 --> 00:12:32.504
Sorry. You got me.

229
00:12:32.587 --> 00:12:34.422
Wow, I didn't expect you to be here.

230
00:12:34.506 --> 00:12:35.674
No, me neither.

231
00:12:36.174 --> 00:12:37.842
What can I do for you?

232
00:12:37.926 --> 00:12:41.930
Well, I just wondered if you'd mind
helping me pick out a fancy suit?

233
00:12:42.889 --> 00:12:45.892
Abso-fucking-lutely.
Perfect timing, actually.

234
00:12:45.976 --> 00:12:48.311
I've gotta pick up some outfits
for this photo shoot I'm doing.

235
00:12:48.395 --> 00:12:49.479
Come with.

236
00:12:49.563 --> 00:12:51.398
-What, now?
-Now.

237
00:12:51.481 --> 00:12:53.483
Let's go kill two birds with one stone.

238
00:12:54.484 --> 00:12:57.696
All right, yeah. Let's go…
murder some birds with a rock.

239
00:12:59.197 --> 00:13:00.323
That was good.

240
00:13:00.407 --> 00:13:01.658
-Yeah?
-Yeah!

241
00:13:01.741 --> 00:13:03.868
-I got attacked by a bird once.
-Did you?

242
00:13:14.754 --> 00:13:17.924
Young man, I think you're late for class

243
00:13:18.508 --> 00:13:20.886
by about 25 years.

244
00:13:25.974 --> 00:13:27.309
Would you like a lollipop?

245
00:13:27.976 --> 00:13:28.977
No.

246
00:13:34.065 --> 00:13:36.026
It's Coach Kent, which can only mean

247
00:13:36.109 --> 00:13:39.112
nobody told him it's a half-day
and Phoebe's mom picked her up hours ago.

248
00:13:39.738 --> 00:13:41.031
Fu…

249
00:13:42.824 --> 00:13:44.034
…n.

250
00:13:44.743 --> 00:13:45.869
That's fun, innit?

251
00:13:47.662 --> 00:13:49.414
Okay. See you later.

252
00:13:54.836 --> 00:13:56.963
I always thought this was
what the teachers did when we went home.

253
00:13:57.047 --> 00:13:58.590
Art fundraiser tonight.

254
00:13:59.174 --> 00:14:00.717
For 20 quid, you can buy a kid's art.

255
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.678
For 40, I'll send it home with you
already in a rubbish bin.

256
00:14:05.055 --> 00:14:06.389
That's a solid business model.

257
00:14:08.642 --> 00:14:10.101
Which one of these is Phoebe's?

258
00:14:11.019 --> 00:14:13.063
Oh, I won't be able to display
Phoebe's artwork.

259
00:14:13.647 --> 00:14:14.981
Why not?

260
00:14:23.865 --> 00:14:25.033
Oh, no.

261
00:14:29.704 --> 00:14:30.622
She draws ti--

262
00:14:30.705 --> 00:14:34.042
Unnervingly accurate
charcoal sketches of breasts, yes.

263
00:14:34.668 --> 00:14:36.419
There were more,
but some of the boys stole them

264
00:14:36.503 --> 00:14:38.004
and I think are using them as currency.

265
00:14:38.838 --> 00:14:40.048
Bloody hell.

266
00:14:42.968 --> 00:14:43.969
Nice.

267
00:14:45.929 --> 00:14:48.056
-Do you need a hand?
-Yep.

268
00:14:59.943 --> 00:15:01.069
Unless you need to go.

269
00:15:04.281 --> 00:15:05.365
No, I got time.

270
00:15:10.078 --> 00:15:11.496
It's show-and-tell today.

271
00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.541
Should I bring my Jamie Tartt jersey
or my LEGO Hogwarts?

272
00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.294
I gotta go with the Jamie Tartt jersey

273
00:15:17.377 --> 00:15:19.462
for fear of how Hogwarts might travel,
you know?

274
00:15:19.546 --> 00:15:21.464
Good thinkin', Abe Lincoln.

275
00:15:23.133 --> 00:15:26.303
Hey, buddy, I gotta let you go, okay?
Have a great day at school. I love you.

276
00:15:26.386 --> 00:15:27.387
Love you.

277
00:15:28.555 --> 00:15:29.639
Hey, boss. What's up?

278
00:15:30.473 --> 00:15:32.350
Right, I'm just gonna come out and say it.

279
00:15:32.434 --> 00:15:34.019
I had a torrid affair with Sam.

280
00:15:34.102 --> 00:15:35.645
Dad, I'm still on.

281
00:15:36.855 --> 00:15:38.398
Hey, sorry about that.

282
00:15:38.481 --> 00:15:39.983
-Okay, I'll talk to you later.
-Bye, Dad.

283
00:15:41.943 --> 00:15:42.944
Yeah.

284
00:15:44.738 --> 00:15:46.197
Okay, so let's see.

285
00:15:46.281 --> 00:15:48.116
-You and--
-Sam.

286
00:15:48.199 --> 00:15:49.826
…uel L. Jackson?

287
00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:52.913
-Obisanya.
-Right, okay. Just checking.

288
00:15:53.747 --> 00:15:56.958
Okay, well, you know,
I think that's great.

289
00:15:57.042 --> 00:15:58.251
Hold on.

290
00:15:58.335 --> 00:15:59.419
Wait. No--

291
00:15:59.502 --> 00:16:00.879
Yes. Yeah, I do. No, I think that's fine.

292
00:16:02.464 --> 00:16:04.549
-I think I need to end it.
-Sure, I can see that.

293
00:16:04.633 --> 00:16:08.303
I asked him for a bit of time
to figure things out.

294
00:16:08.803 --> 00:16:10.513
And now we're in
a bit of a limbo situation.

295
00:16:10.597 --> 00:16:12.933
Great party game,
horrible relationship status.

296
00:16:13.016 --> 00:16:15.685
And then Edwin Akufo swoops in
to take him away,

297
00:16:15.769 --> 00:16:17.771
and I've lost all objectivity.

298
00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:21.691
Sam's a really great player.

299
00:16:21.775 --> 00:16:23.026
One of the best we got.

300
00:16:23.777 --> 00:16:25.862
But do I want him to stay
because of my feelings for him?

301
00:16:25.946 --> 00:16:26.988
Good question.

302
00:16:28.531 --> 00:16:30.951
-We really were great together.
-I mean, come on.

303
00:16:31.034 --> 00:16:33.620
Sam and Rebecca are already
one of my all-time favorite TV couples.

304
00:16:33.703 --> 00:16:36.373
To have one of them in real life?
Yes, please.

305
00:16:36.456 --> 00:16:38.875
But if he wants to go,
I shouldn't stand in his way.

306
00:16:38.959 --> 00:16:40.210
I could not agree more.

307
00:16:40.293 --> 00:16:43.505
But if I let him go,
I might regret it for the rest of my life.

308
00:16:44.339 --> 00:16:45.674
Turns out, I could agree more.

309
00:16:50.595 --> 00:16:51.930
Well, Rebecca.

310
00:16:53.098 --> 00:16:54.099
Listen to me.

311
00:16:58.478 --> 00:16:59.479
Don't listen to me.

312
00:17:00.855 --> 00:17:02.148
Don't listen to Edwin Akufo.

313
00:17:02.232 --> 00:17:03.692
Don't even listen to Sam.

314
00:17:03.775 --> 00:17:05.193
You just listen to your gut, okay?

315
00:17:06.945 --> 00:17:09.613
And on your way down to your gut,
check in with your heart.

316
00:17:09.698 --> 00:17:11.992
Between those two things,
they'll let you know what's what.

317
00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.329
They make good harmony,

318
00:17:16.412 --> 00:17:18.832
like two-thirds of Bone Thugs-N-Harmony,
you know what I mean?

319
00:17:22.334 --> 00:17:23.335
Thank you, Ted.

320
00:17:27.215 --> 00:17:29.551
You know, boss, you're starting to develop
a bit of a habit.

321
00:17:30.594 --> 00:17:31.928
-Am I?
-Oh, yeah.

322
00:17:32.512 --> 00:17:35.557
Same time, same place last year,
you dropped another truth bomb on me.

323
00:17:40.103 --> 00:17:42.355
-See you next year.
-I can't wait.

324
00:17:56.244 --> 00:17:59.831
Oh, my God.
That's so good, I can't even look at you.

325
00:18:00.582 --> 00:18:01.625
Thanks, Jacques-o.

326
00:18:02.334 --> 00:18:04.836
Oi, how you doing in there, babe?

327
00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.755
God, this place is so posh.

328
00:18:06.838 --> 00:18:08.715
Feel like I'm not supposed to be here.

329
00:18:08.798 --> 00:18:10.383
This place is for rich twats

330
00:18:10.467 --> 00:18:13.136
who piss away all their money
on an outfit they only wear once.

331
00:18:14.512 --> 00:18:17.307
But, Nate,
today you are one of those twats.

332
00:18:18.141 --> 00:18:19.267
I quite like that.

333
00:18:19.351 --> 00:18:21.269
-Oh, this is so much fun.
-Yeah.

334
00:18:21.353 --> 00:18:23.063
Roy never does this stuff with me.

335
00:18:23.772 --> 00:18:26.316
He's always like, "I'm Roy Kent."

336
00:18:27.192 --> 00:18:28.902
"Why do I need to go shopping?

337
00:18:28.985 --> 00:18:31.696
I already own a black T-shirt and jeans."

338
00:18:36.243 --> 00:18:38.662
This is yes.

339
00:18:39.996 --> 00:18:41.373
But I'm worried about the crotch.

340
00:18:41.456 --> 00:18:44.751
Does the crotch feel loose?
The crotch looks loose.

341
00:18:44.834 --> 00:18:46.545
Keeley, thoughts on the crotch?

342
00:18:50.715 --> 00:18:51.841
Oh, my Go--

343
00:18:57.264 --> 00:18:58.807
I think the crotch looks great.

344
00:18:59.391 --> 00:19:00.892
We can have the crotch taken in.

345
00:19:00.976 --> 00:19:04.104
It's better to have a tight crotch
than a loose crotch, you know?

346
00:19:04.729 --> 00:19:06.565
But we love the suit, yes?

347
00:19:08.733 --> 00:19:10.652
I-- What do you think?

348
00:19:12.571 --> 00:19:14.114
No, I don't think this is it.

349
00:19:14.197 --> 00:19:16.408
-No.
-Take it off immediately.

350
00:19:17.367 --> 00:19:18.577
Would you guys like a drink?

351
00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:20.245
Oh, yeah, go on.

352
00:19:20.328 --> 00:19:21.580
Glass of champagne?

353
00:19:21.663 --> 00:19:22.789
I'm all right, thanks.

354
00:19:22.872 --> 00:19:25.542
Oi, it's free.

355
00:19:25.625 --> 00:19:26.710
And…

356
00:19:26.793 --> 00:19:30.380
when you see the prices,
you're gonna wish you'd drank more of it.

357
00:19:30.463 --> 00:19:32.090
Oh, my God. Yeah.

358
00:19:32.173 --> 00:19:34.050
A whiskey, thank you. Please.

359
00:19:38.013 --> 00:19:39.431
Knock knock, Doc Doc.

360
00:19:40.807 --> 00:19:43.393
Oh, please don't tell me
you're taking my office now.

361
00:19:43.476 --> 00:19:44.686
What. No, no. I just came up

362
00:19:44.769 --> 00:19:47.272
to invite Doctor Sharon
to Colin's birthday party tomorrow night.

363
00:19:49.232 --> 00:19:51.067
Colin's birthday is August the 21st.

364
00:19:51.151 --> 00:19:52.652
I love that you know that.

365
00:19:52.736 --> 00:19:54.237
Yeah, I know everybody's birthday.

366
00:19:54.321 --> 00:19:55.572
Really?

367
00:19:56.948 --> 00:19:58.658
-Liam Neeson.
-June 7th.

368
00:19:58.742 --> 00:20:00.577
-Tina Turner.
-November 26th.

369
00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.204
Chuck Norris, Sharon Stone,
and Osama Bin Laden.

370
00:20:04.372 --> 00:20:05.749
All March the 10th.

371
00:20:06.333 --> 00:20:07.626
You are good. And you're right.

372
00:20:07.709 --> 00:20:10.420
Colin's party was just a cover story
for Sharon's going-away party.

373
00:20:10.503 --> 00:20:11.463
Not bad, huh?

374
00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:15.675
I hate to be the bearer of bad news,
Ted, but Sharon's already gone.

375
00:20:15.759 --> 00:20:19.179
Beg to differ, Higgy Stardust.
Sharon's last day is mañana.

376
00:20:19.262 --> 00:20:22.933
Yes, but an emergency came up,
and she has to leave tonight.

377
00:20:24.226 --> 00:20:25.727
Wait, she left without saying goodbye?

378
00:20:27.145 --> 00:20:29.356
She wrote everybody a letter.

379
00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.608
Mine was very nice.

380
00:20:33.235 --> 00:20:34.486
Here's yours.

381
00:20:36.029 --> 00:20:37.030
No.

382
00:20:39.241 --> 00:20:41.868
Don't let her get away with it, Ted!

383
00:20:43.745 --> 00:20:44.788
Yes.

384
00:20:49.292 --> 00:20:51.795
-Wow.
-I know, right?

385
00:20:54.089 --> 00:20:55.173
Kelechi Nwaneri.

386
00:20:56.049 --> 00:20:57.384
Yeah, his work is incredible.

387
00:20:57.467 --> 00:20:59.553
Well, he's Nigerian.

388
00:21:01.304 --> 00:21:02.305
I just bought it.

389
00:21:03.515 --> 00:21:06.309
So I can donate it
to the Cape Coast Castle Museum in Ghana.

390
00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.895
This piece belongs in Africa.

391
00:21:12.023 --> 00:21:13.108
It's amazing.

392
00:21:13.191 --> 00:21:14.818
Even for a Nigerian.

393
00:21:20.657 --> 00:21:23.326
Sam, I'm a walking confliction.

394
00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.453
I am a billionaire,

395
00:21:25.954 --> 00:21:28.582
yet I don't believe
billionaires should exist.

396
00:21:29.749 --> 00:21:32.752
That's why I'm breaking up
my father's empire.

397
00:21:33.253 --> 00:21:35.380
I'm using the money to make better things

398
00:21:36.506 --> 00:21:38.508
and hopefully make things better.

399
00:21:41.803 --> 00:21:43.513
You are not at all what I expected.

400
00:21:44.723 --> 00:21:46.641
You don't even have a security detail.

401
00:21:47.642 --> 00:21:49.227
Okay.

402
00:21:49.311 --> 00:21:51.813
That's because
I bought out the entire museum

403
00:21:51.897 --> 00:21:53.773
and filled it with actors.

404
00:21:57.611 --> 00:22:01.156
Oh, I thought I recognized him
from I May Destroy You.

405
00:22:03.658 --> 00:22:04.743
Are you hungry?

406
00:22:04.826 --> 00:22:05.827
Starving.

407
00:22:05.911 --> 00:22:07.245
I know a perfect place.

408
00:22:07.329 --> 00:22:09.289
-Edwin.
-It's good to see you.

409
00:22:09.372 --> 00:22:11.416
-This is my friend, Sam.
-Hey, you all right?

410
00:22:11.499 --> 00:22:12.751
Lovely to meet you.

411
00:22:12.834 --> 00:22:14.878
Congratulations.
You both just met a cool person.

412
00:22:15.670 --> 00:22:16.671
Cheers.

413
00:22:16.755 --> 00:22:17.756
See you.

414
00:22:19.424 --> 00:22:21.426
-Pretty cool, eh?
-What?

415
00:22:21.509 --> 00:22:23.345
-That was Banksy.
-Banksy?

416
00:22:23.428 --> 00:22:24.429
Yeah.

417
00:22:24.512 --> 00:22:26.223
-The--
-Yes.

418
00:22:26.306 --> 00:22:27.766
Oh, my God.

419
00:22:30.435 --> 00:22:31.436
Sorry.

420
00:22:32.938 --> 00:22:34.814
Yeah, let's do it. Thanks, babe.

421
00:22:37.692 --> 00:22:38.902
Fuck me!

422
00:22:38.985 --> 00:22:40.487
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

423
00:22:40.570 --> 00:22:42.364
You look so hot.

424
00:22:42.447 --> 00:22:44.032
I just wanna fix your tie really quick.

425
00:22:44.115 --> 00:22:45.951
Come here. Okay.

426
00:22:47.452 --> 00:22:49.996
Thank you so much, by the way.

427
00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:51.998
You're so good at everything,

428
00:22:52.082 --> 00:22:55.627
and you're always helping people
and making things better.

429
00:22:56.836 --> 00:22:57.879
Just like you.

430
00:23:00.507 --> 00:23:01.716
-Sorry.
-It's all right.

431
00:23:02.300 --> 00:23:03.301
Do you ever--

432
00:23:03.385 --> 00:23:05.345
Do you ever feel like
you wanna be the boss?

433
00:23:07.931 --> 00:23:09.766
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

434
00:23:09.849 --> 00:23:13.103
I mean, I did used to worry that
I was gonna end up like my mum.

435
00:23:14.271 --> 00:23:16.982
She spent years working
at the same company tirelessly

436
00:23:17.065 --> 00:23:18.817
just for a man to take all the credit.

437
00:23:19.568 --> 00:23:21.319
She wasn't brave enough to dream big.

438
00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:25.407
So, I decided to do things
very differently.

439
00:23:26.324 --> 00:23:27.867
And then I met Rebecca,

440
00:23:28.743 --> 00:23:31.079
and she inspired me to wanna be a boss.

441
00:23:33.206 --> 00:23:35.542
People like you and I,
we can't help but dream big.

442
00:23:36.793 --> 00:23:40.463
And no one is gonna fight harder
for their dreams than us, right?

443
00:23:40.547 --> 00:23:41.548
Right.

444
00:23:43.508 --> 00:23:46.386
The scariest part of all of it is
making the decision to just go for it.

445
00:23:46.469 --> 00:23:49.598
'Cause once you do that,
then everything just sort of falls in--

446
00:23:54.144 --> 00:23:56.521
God. I'm so sorry. I didn't--

447
00:23:56.605 --> 00:23:57.772
-That's okay.
-No, it's not.

448
00:23:57.856 --> 00:24:00.066
-Yes, it is. Don't worry about it.
-No. No, it's fine--

449
00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:01.151
-It was--
-No, it was--

450
00:24:01.234 --> 00:24:03.570
-It happens sometimes to the best of us.
-It's not--

451
00:24:04.362 --> 00:24:05.488
-I just--
-I--

452
00:24:05.572 --> 00:24:06.948
God, I'm gonna get outta this--

453
00:24:07.032 --> 00:24:08.992
-Don't worry about it.
-I do worry about it.

454
00:24:09.075 --> 00:24:10.118
Don't.

455
00:24:10.201 --> 00:24:11.453
Shit.

456
00:24:34.684 --> 00:24:36.519
Is that a younger year?

457
00:24:36.603 --> 00:24:37.812
Nope, same year.

458
00:24:39.147 --> 00:24:40.690
Then why are their pictures shit,

459
00:24:40.774 --> 00:24:43.068
and yours are… not shit?

460
00:24:43.985 --> 00:24:46.321
Well, I take the pictures
before they can fuck them up.

461
00:24:46.404 --> 00:24:48.698
They hate it,
but I know it's for the best.

462
00:24:49.532 --> 00:24:51.743
So you're Ms. Bowen, the mean teacher.

463
00:24:53.078 --> 00:24:54.663
Well, Phoebe likes you.

464
00:24:54.746 --> 00:24:56.831
She's smart. Most of them hate me.

465
00:24:56.915 --> 00:24:59.751
They have, like,
20 different mean nicknames for me.

466
00:24:59.834 --> 00:25:00.877
Go on.

467
00:25:00.961 --> 00:25:02.128
I don't know any of them.

468
00:25:05.298 --> 00:25:09.761
Ms. Bowlegs, Ms. Boring, Ms. Bonehead,
Ms. Bellend, Boaty Ms. Boatface

469
00:25:09.844 --> 00:25:12.847
and then there's one little boy
who simply calls me Fuck-witch,

470
00:25:12.931 --> 00:25:16.351
which is admittedly my favorite.

471
00:25:16.434 --> 00:25:19.813
Well, best teachers are the toughest ones.

472
00:25:19.896 --> 00:25:22.732
My first coach used to
chase me round the pitch on a motorbike

473
00:25:22.816 --> 00:25:24.359
like we were in fucking Mad Max.

474
00:25:24.442 --> 00:25:25.694
That's terrifying.

475
00:25:25.777 --> 00:25:27.571
Yeah, but it made me fast.

476
00:25:30.615 --> 00:25:32.075
The half-hour countdown begins.

477
00:25:33.076 --> 00:25:34.494
Nothing worse than parents' mixers.

478
00:25:34.578 --> 00:25:37.205
They get free chardonnay,
and I get to ward off all the single dads.

479
00:25:38.373 --> 00:25:40.584
-And not-so-single dads.
-Right.

480
00:25:40.667 --> 00:25:41.668
Are you married?

481
00:25:42.377 --> 00:25:43.378
No.

482
00:25:56.057 --> 00:25:58.268
-I've gotta go.
-You're not gonna stay for the art show?

483
00:25:58.351 --> 00:25:59.686
No, sorry.

484
00:26:02.606 --> 00:26:03.982
Thanks for all your help.

485
00:26:10.071 --> 00:26:11.823
Karen, for God's sake, grow the fuck up.

486
00:26:19.831 --> 00:26:22.334
Well, well, well.
Look what the weird bike rode in.

487
00:26:23.501 --> 00:26:25.670
Ted, how long have you
been standing out here?

488
00:26:25.754 --> 00:26:26.922
A long time.

489
00:26:27.005 --> 00:26:28.465
And I really gotta use the john too,

490
00:26:28.548 --> 00:26:31.343
but I'm gonna hold it a bit longer,
'cause I'm so dang ticked off at you.

491
00:26:35.222 --> 00:26:37.349
I was right.
It's a lot easier to navigate that hallway

492
00:26:37.432 --> 00:26:38.600
with this thing all folded up.

493
00:26:39.643 --> 00:26:40.477
Thank you for carrying it up.

494
00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:41.853
How could you just leave?

495
00:26:42.979 --> 00:26:44.606
Sorry, I'm not good with goodbyes.

496
00:26:44.689 --> 00:26:47.067
Well, when I was a baby,
I wasn't good at walking and talking,

497
00:26:47.150 --> 00:26:48.652
but I stuck with it and look at me now.

498
00:26:48.735 --> 00:26:50.445
-Did you get my letter?
-Yes.

499
00:26:50.528 --> 00:26:51.529
-Did you read it?
-No!

500
00:26:51.613 --> 00:26:53.281
We had a whole thing planned for you.

501
00:26:53.365 --> 00:26:55.533
You know how hard it is to get
grown men to learn choreography?

502
00:26:55.617 --> 00:26:58.912
Almost impossible.
Heck, we even got you a gift.

503
00:27:01.206 --> 00:27:02.791
Spoiler alert, it's a bunch of cash.

504
00:27:03.375 --> 00:27:04.584
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

505
00:27:05.085 --> 00:27:06.503
But, Ted, you knew I was leaving.

506
00:27:06.586 --> 00:27:09.172
I did, but I thought I was gonna get
a chance to say goodbye to you.

507
00:27:09.923 --> 00:27:12.592
My wife left me, my dad left me,

508
00:27:12.676 --> 00:27:16.429
and you, more than anyone in the world,
knows how I feel when I get abandoned,

509
00:27:16.513 --> 00:27:17.973
and you just left.

510
00:27:18.557 --> 00:27:20.976
I wrote about that.
It's all in the letter I left for you.

511
00:27:21.059 --> 00:27:24.020
Wait a minute. Okay.
You mean this? This right here?

512
00:27:24.104 --> 00:27:26.940
Guess what. I'm not gonna read
your letter, ever, okay?

513
00:27:27.023 --> 00:27:29.150
You got something to say to me,
just say it to my face.

514
00:27:30.569 --> 00:27:32.028
I thought we had a breakthrough.

515
00:27:32.112 --> 00:27:34.030
You did.
You confronted things you had--

516
00:27:34.114 --> 00:27:36.366
No, no, no. Not me. I'm talking about us.

517
00:27:37.742 --> 00:27:39.869
-We did, Ted.
-Yeah.

518
00:27:39.953 --> 00:27:41.746
Thanks to you, I've learned that

519
00:27:41.830 --> 00:27:45.166
expressing my vulnerabilities can help
my patients with theirs.

520
00:27:45.250 --> 00:27:47.586
You helped me become a better therapist.

521
00:27:49.004 --> 00:27:51.631
And that's saying something,
because I was already fucking brilliant.

522
00:27:55.051 --> 00:27:56.094
That's nice of you to say.

523
00:27:57.679 --> 00:28:00.432
And yet, you were gonna leave
without letting me know any of that.

524
00:28:00.932 --> 00:28:03.268
-Ted, it's all in the letter.
-It's all in the letter!

525
00:28:03.351 --> 00:28:06.646
It's all in your-- Okay, well, fine.
I'll read your stupid-ass letter.

526
00:28:06.730 --> 00:28:07.856
Unbelievable.

527
00:28:11.359 --> 00:28:12.527
You spelled "favorite" wrong.

528
00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:01.368
It's a very good letter.

529
00:29:03.745 --> 00:29:07.123
I feel more comfortable writing goodbye
than saying it. I'm sorry.

530
00:29:09.626 --> 00:29:11.294
It's okay. I understand.

531
00:29:14.965 --> 00:29:17.050
My train to Royston doesn't leave
till midnight.

532
00:29:17.592 --> 00:29:18.802
Wanna grab a drink?

533
00:29:21.221 --> 00:29:22.347
I'm buying.

534
00:29:25.225 --> 00:29:26.601
Yeah, okay. That'd be nice. Yeah.

535
00:29:28.436 --> 00:29:31.314
-But I really gotta pee first. I gotta--
-Door to the left.

536
00:29:39.573 --> 00:29:41.908
I've never had
West African food this good in London.

537
00:29:41.992 --> 00:29:44.160
I can't believe
I didn't know this place existed.

538
00:29:44.744 --> 00:29:45.996
Well, it doesn't.

539
00:29:46.496 --> 00:29:47.831
I had it created for us.

540
00:29:48.415 --> 00:29:49.583
I brought in my own chefs.

541
00:29:50.542 --> 00:29:51.751
I travel often,

542
00:29:52.377 --> 00:29:55.171
and I know what it's like
to miss the food from home.

543
00:29:58.383 --> 00:29:59.593
Actors?

544
00:29:59.676 --> 00:30:00.677
Friends.

545
00:30:06.349 --> 00:30:08.226
Listen. I wanna be honest with you.

546
00:30:09.978 --> 00:30:12.355
I don't see myself leaving
Richmond to play for…

547
00:30:12.939 --> 00:30:15.650
well, whatever team
you end up owning one day.

548
00:30:18.486 --> 00:30:23.450
Sam, you are
the fourth person to know this.

549
00:30:24.367 --> 00:30:26.953
I'm buying Raja Casablanca in Morocco.

550
00:30:28.413 --> 00:30:32.042
My only focus in life will be to make us
one of the biggest clubs in the world.

551
00:30:33.460 --> 00:30:38.215
Bayern, United, PSG, Barcelona…

552
00:30:40.008 --> 00:30:41.176
Casablanca.

553
00:30:45.305 --> 00:30:48.516
The greatest African players
around the world will come home

554
00:30:48.600 --> 00:30:49.684
to play for us.

555
00:30:51.102 --> 00:30:55.774
Mark my words, in 20 years,
an African team will win the World Cup.

556
00:30:57.108 --> 00:31:01.112
Sam, you inspired the world
to care about what's happening at home.

557
00:31:02.405 --> 00:31:04.658
That's why I want you to come play for me.

558
00:31:04.741 --> 00:31:08.662
I want the incredible man you are,
not the footballer.

559
00:31:10.664 --> 00:31:12.332
Although the footballer too is incredible.

560
00:31:15.710 --> 00:31:16.711
Thank you.

561
00:31:18.838 --> 00:31:22.300
I mean…
You've given me a lot to think about.

562
00:31:22.968 --> 00:31:25.136
Please. Take all the time you need.

563
00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:29.015
You have 72 hours.

564
00:31:31.851 --> 00:31:33.895
Hey, please. Finish the jollof. Huh?

565
00:31:33.979 --> 00:31:35.146
I insist.

566
00:31:35.730 --> 00:31:39.317
Thank you. You know, I appreciate
that you had it made the Nigerian way.

567
00:31:39.901 --> 00:31:43.363
Well, I thought you'd prefer it,
even though the Ghanaian way is better.

568
00:31:43.446 --> 00:31:46.241
Oh, I know we've been getting along,
but I will fight you on this one.

569
00:31:46.324 --> 00:31:47.576
Let us fight then.

570
00:31:53.248 --> 00:31:54.749
Oh, wonderful, Mr. Kent.

571
00:31:54.833 --> 00:31:57.460
We've got you upstairs.
You'll start in the black suit,

572
00:31:57.544 --> 00:32:00.964
and then we'd love for Nicky
to take a pass at your eyebrows.

573
00:32:08.138 --> 00:32:09.806
Hey. I'm sorry I'm late.

574
00:32:09.890 --> 00:32:12.684
You're not late, babe.
Your outfit's in the closet.

575
00:32:13.435 --> 00:32:14.644
You look cool as fuck.

576
00:32:15.687 --> 00:32:16.688
Thank you.

577
00:32:19.149 --> 00:32:20.942
How was suit shopping with Nate?

578
00:32:21.026 --> 00:32:22.193
Yeah, it was fine.

579
00:32:27.198 --> 00:32:30.994
I know that you hate this stuff, babe,
but it's gonna be good, yeah?

580
00:32:31.077 --> 00:32:34.664
Please say that it's gonna be good
'cause I'm really losing it.

581
00:32:34.748 --> 00:32:36.041
I'm so nervous.

582
00:32:37.667 --> 00:32:41.004
Babe, you've done a thousand magazines.

583
00:32:41.087 --> 00:32:43.006
You did an advert for a service station

584
00:32:43.089 --> 00:32:46.593
where you jumped out of an airplane
topless eating a hamburger.

585
00:32:47.427 --> 00:32:49.512
You can't be more nervous than that.

586
00:32:50.972 --> 00:32:52.349
But this isn't that.

587
00:32:54.142 --> 00:32:55.685
It was about how I looked.

588
00:32:56.519 --> 00:32:57.979
This is about me.

589
00:32:59.522 --> 00:33:02.150
I had to do an interview,
like a real interview.

590
00:33:02.234 --> 00:33:04.945
They asked me
about my thoughts and my feelings

591
00:33:05.028 --> 00:33:07.322
and my goals for the future.

592
00:33:10.116 --> 00:33:12.535
When people read this article,
they're gonna see me.

593
00:33:12.619 --> 00:33:13.828
See the real me.

594
00:33:22.921 --> 00:33:26.132
The real you is fucking amazing.

595
00:33:27.300 --> 00:33:29.719
And now the whole world
is gonna get to see that.

596
00:33:31.054 --> 00:33:34.140
You are Keeley fucking Jones,

597
00:33:34.724 --> 00:33:36.184
the independent woman.

598
00:33:37.477 --> 00:33:39.020
You're gonna kill it.

599
00:33:43.108 --> 00:33:44.568
So I should keep my top on?

600
00:33:45.777 --> 00:33:46.778
Maybe for one shot.

601
00:33:51.366 --> 00:33:52.701
Thank you.

602
00:34:29.362 --> 00:34:30.572
Hello, Dad.

603
00:34:31.615 --> 00:34:32.657
Yeah.

604
00:34:34.034 --> 00:34:35.242
It was incredible.

605
00:34:36.077 --> 00:34:39.539
Yeah, yeah, he took me to a museum.
And then we had Nigerian food.

606
00:34:47.797 --> 00:34:51.343
Okay, great.
And now look at one another.

607
00:34:53.094 --> 00:34:54.095
Come on then.

608
00:35:03.813 --> 00:35:07.400
That's wonderful.
Can I get the 85, please?

609
00:35:08.276 --> 00:35:10.528
Switching lenses. Will only be a second.

610
00:35:11.112 --> 00:35:12.113
Yeah.

611
00:35:15.367 --> 00:35:17.911
All right, so, earlier
when I was suit shopping with Nate,

612
00:35:17.994 --> 00:35:19.746
there was a little misunderstanding.

613
00:35:19.829 --> 00:35:21.164
He tried to kiss me.

614
00:35:22.040 --> 00:35:23.333
It wasn't a big deal,

615
00:35:24.417 --> 00:35:26.836
but I just thought you should know.

616
00:35:26.920 --> 00:35:29.798
Shit. That must've been awkward.

617
00:35:32.050 --> 00:35:33.218
Thank you for telling me.

618
00:35:40.600 --> 00:35:44.688
I was talking to Phoebe's teacher earlier
for three hours.

619
00:35:45.272 --> 00:35:47.732
And at the end she asked me
if I was married, and I just said no,

620
00:35:47.816 --> 00:35:49.192
nothing else.

621
00:35:49.276 --> 00:35:50.277
I don't know why.

622
00:36:03.915 --> 00:36:05.375
At the funeral,

623
00:36:06.501 --> 00:36:08.628
Jamie told me he still loves me.

624
00:36:16.303 --> 00:36:18.847
Okay. Here we go.

625
00:36:24.019 --> 00:36:25.270
Turn to me.

626
00:36:41.328 --> 00:36:44.164
Well, well, well. Look who knows her way
around a pinball machine, huh?

627
00:36:44.247 --> 00:36:46.041
-I love pinball.
-Yeah.

628
00:36:46.124 --> 00:36:48.752
It's one of the most entertaining
forms of meditation.

629
00:36:48.835 --> 00:36:51.588
Your only opponent is
yourself and gravity.

630
00:36:52.547 --> 00:36:54.799
Yeah, two things we're stuck with.

631
00:36:54.883 --> 00:36:57.469
At least until that Elon Musk fella
stops messing about on Twitter

632
00:36:57.552 --> 00:36:58.845
and starts focusing on jet packs.

633
00:37:01.431 --> 00:37:03.266
"SMF," huh?

634
00:37:03.350 --> 00:37:04.559
Oh, let me guess.

635
00:37:06.228 --> 00:37:07.812
Sharon Mildred Fieldstone?

636
00:37:08.396 --> 00:37:09.522
Sexy motherfucker.

637
00:37:10.273 --> 00:37:12.067
Rest in peace, Mr. Nelson.

638
00:37:15.612 --> 00:37:16.947
-Another round?
-Oh, yeah. Come on.

639
00:37:17.030 --> 00:37:18.031
Come on now.

640
00:37:18.531 --> 00:37:20.659
This one's gonna be on me.
Actually, you know what? No.

641
00:37:20.742 --> 00:37:22.744
Still gonna be on you, Dr. Moneybags.

642
00:37:22.827 --> 00:37:25.872
If you excuse me, I'm gonna go hit
one of my favorite British words,

643
00:37:25.956 --> 00:37:28.667
and my absolute favorite Diamond Phillips,
the loo.

644
00:37:30.126 --> 00:37:31.503
Another two, please, Mae.

645
00:37:31.586 --> 00:37:33.588
-Okey dokey.
-Thank you.

646
00:37:36.800 --> 00:37:38.385
You're the shrink for the team, yeah?

647
00:37:40.053 --> 00:37:41.471
Go on. Ask her.

648
00:37:42.055 --> 00:37:43.056
I'm scared of snakes.

649
00:37:43.932 --> 00:37:46.977
Like, really scared of snakes,
even the tiny ones in my garden.

650
00:37:47.477 --> 00:37:48.645
Does that mean anything?

651
00:37:48.728 --> 00:37:50.480
Do you want it to mean something?

652
00:37:51.690 --> 00:37:54.234
I just don't wanna be afraid
when I'm tending to my tomatoes.

653
00:37:55.193 --> 00:37:57.070
Because the garden is your safe space.

654
00:37:59.239 --> 00:38:00.407
Is it about the snakes,

655
00:38:00.490 --> 00:38:04.077
or is it about the fear and anxiety
slithering into your consciousness?

656
00:38:04.786 --> 00:38:05.787
That's it.

657
00:38:05.870 --> 00:38:07.998
The last one! That's it!

658
00:38:08.081 --> 00:38:09.124
Sorceress.

659
00:38:10.333 --> 00:38:12.210
-I have a recurring dream…
-Oh, God.

660
00:38:12.294 --> 00:38:13.962
…where I'm floating.

661
00:38:14.045 --> 00:38:16.381
Not flying, floating.

662
00:38:18.049 --> 00:38:19.217
Piss off, you three.

663
00:38:19.801 --> 00:38:23.096
You want psychiatric help,
call the number I gave you.

664
00:38:24.431 --> 00:38:25.432
Think about it.

665
00:38:26.016 --> 00:38:27.017
Thanks.

666
00:38:28.852 --> 00:38:30.770
-Thanks, Mae.
-There you go, love.

667
00:38:31.479 --> 00:38:32.689
Oh, no. I ordered two.

668
00:38:33.481 --> 00:38:35.066
Ted asked me to give you this.

669
00:38:45.702 --> 00:38:48.079
Son of a bitch stole my move.

670
00:38:58.215 --> 00:39:00.133
Here's one with no shit in it.

671
00:39:01.426 --> 00:39:02.427
Thanks.

672
00:39:25.492 --> 00:39:27.327
I can't give you an answer about us.

673
00:39:30.080 --> 00:39:33.583
And I know I can't ask you not to go.

674
00:39:38.964 --> 00:39:40.423
But I hope you don't go.

675
00:39:45.011 --> 00:39:46.221
I should go.

